Stackchan Gemini firmware
=========================

This project is a derivative work of **stackchan-idf**, an ESP-IDF firmware
for M5Stack CoreS3 Stack-chan written by Kenta IDA.

  Upstream:  https://github.com/ciniml/stackchan-idf
  Fork used: https://github.com/mongonta0716/stackchan-idf
  License:   Boost Software License 1.0

The overwhelming majority of the source in this repository — the avatar
renderer and its DSL virtual machine, the SCS0009 servo driver, the CoreS3
board bring-up, the Gemini Live conversation client, the BLE GATT and Wi-Fi
HTTP settings services, and the build system — is Kenta IDA's work, carried
over under the Boost Software License 1.0 and still carrying its original
SPDX headers.

Changes made in this repository relative to upstream:

  * Gemini Live is the only conversation backend. The OpenAI Realtime,
    XiaoZhi and local-PC-server backends and their configuration surfaces
    were removed.
  * An ambient status HUD composited over the avatar face, plus a
    human-first rewrite of the on-device Chat and Info tabs.
  * The feature set was cut back to four things — face, LED control, Gemini
    conversation and servo control — by removing NFC/PN532, the GC0308
    camera and QR scanner, Wi-Fi RTP audio receive, BLE audio streaming,
    the Telegram probe, the lightning-talk timer, the AtomS3R board variant
    and assorted bring-up diagnostics.

Stackchan Gemini is the base tier built on the shared Stack-chan core
(core/, stackchan-core), the robot app collected from Stackchan Roombot and
Stackchan Server Bot by the same author.

